{"id":"ux-what-is-ux","title":"UI/UX: what UX design is","subject":"UI/UX design","label":"UI/UX design","exams":[],"language":"en","seconds":166,"duration":165.66,"audio":"voice.mp3","words":453,"sections":[{"id":"hook","title":"Start here","start":0,"end":12.525},{"id":"explain","title":"UX defined","start":12.525,"end":34.485},{"id":"explain2","title":"UI and process","start":34.485,"end":71.205},{"id":"example","title":"Money apps","start":71.205,"end":88.905},{"id":"check","title":"Quick check","start":88.905,"end":102.945},{"id":"answer","title":"The answer","start":102.945,"end":113.365},{"id":"mistakes","title":"Common mistakes","start":113.365,"end":134.715},{"id":"recap","title":"Recap and tip","start":134.715,"end":165.66}],"lines":[{"s":0,"a":0.5,"b":4.38,"text":"Have you ever used an app that looked lovely, but still made you want to give up?","w":[0.52,0.68,0.86,1.14,1.34,1.52,1.68,1.86,2.14,2.88,3.06,3.38,3.58,3.72,3.86,3.96,4.18]},{"s":0,"a":4.83,"b":5.5,"text":"I'm Kora.","w":[4.94,5.12]},{"s":0,"a":5.8,"b":7.71,"text":"Today we answer a simple question.","w":[5.84,6.28,6.52,6.82,6.96,7.28]},{"s":0,"a":8.01,"b":12.1,"text":"What is UX design, and why does it matter even when the screen looks fine?","w":[8.06,8.28,8.5,8.84,9.7,9.9,10.16,10.32,10.42,10.78,10.98,11.12,11.26,11.54,11.78]},{"s":1,"a":12.95,"b":18.07,"text":"UX means user experience. It is how it feels to use a product from start to finish.","w":[13.16,13.6,13.96,14.22,15.24,15.36,15.52,15.7,15.84,16.18,16.38,16.54,16.62,17,17.24,17.54,17.68]},{"s":1,"a":18.37,"b":24.44,"text":"Good UX asks one question. Can you reach your goal easily, without confusion or wasted effort?","w":[18.4,18.7,19.18,19.6,19.76,20.68,20.84,20.98,21.18,21.36,21.74,22.5,22.8,23.46,23.6,24.06]},{"s":1,"a":24.89,"b":30,"text":"Good UX is useful. It is usable, so it is easy to learn and hard to get wrong.","w":[24.9,25.38,25.9,26.08,26.76,26.88,27.04,27.72,27.9,28,28.2,28.46,28.62,28.98,29.14,29.4,29.5,29.66]},{"s":1,"a":30.3,"b":34.06,"text":"It is also accessible, so people with different abilities can use it too.","w":[30.36,30.46,30.7,31.06,31.92,32.08,32.36,32.54,32.82,33.32,33.54,33.7,33.82]},{"s":2,"a":34.91,"b":39.86,"text":"UI means user interface. That is the screens, buttons, text and colours you see and touch.","w":[35.08,35.4,35.72,35.94,36.84,37.02,37.14,37.24,37.76,38.18,38.5,38.64,39,39.18,39.38,39.5]},{"s":2,"a":40.16,"b":45.52,"text":"UI is one part of UX. A beautiful interface can still give a bad experience.","w":[40.34,40.88,41.14,41.32,41.58,41.76,42.8,42.9,43.38,43.9,44.1,44.4,44.56,44.64,44.88]},{"s":2,"a":45.82,"b":50.77,"text":"Imagine a lovely form that loses everything you typed. It looks good, but it fails you.","w":[45.88,46.32,46.44,46.86,47.14,47.34,47.82,48.2,48.34,49.12,49.22,49.5,49.96,50.12,50.26,50.58]},{"s":2,"a":51.07,"b":59.72,"text":"The UX process is simple to say. Understand the users, define the problem, sketch ideas, prototype, test with real people, and repeat.","w":[51.07,51.28,51.62,52.16,52.3,52.64,52.78,53.42,53.96,54.16,54.8,55.24,55.34,56.08,56.44,57.2,58.02,58.36,58.54,58.82,59.26,59.38]},{"s":2,"a":60.02,"b":65.1,"text":"The designer is not the user. So decisions come from watching users, not guessing.","w":[60.04,60.18,60.8,61,61.24,61.46,62.14,62.3,62.84,63.08,63.3,63.76,64.48,64.72]},{"s":2,"a":65.4,"b":70.78,"text":"Don Norman, who worked at Apple, made the term user experience popular in the nineteen nineties.","w":[65.44,65.78,66.32,66.5,66.82,67.02,67.52,67.74,67.86,68.24,68.52,69.12,69.66,69.74,69.88,70.24]},{"s":3,"a":71.63,"b":76.92,"text":"Take two apps for sending money. The first needs nine taps, and shows a confusing error.","w":[71.64,71.9,72.2,72.42,72.58,72.92,73.74,73.92,74.24,74.56,74.82,75.58,75.76,76.04,76.12,76.66]},{"s":3,"a":77.22,"b":82.55,"text":"The second needs three taps, confirms the name of the receiver, and says clearly what went wrong.","w":[77.24,77.42,77.82,78.18,78.48,78.96,79.44,79.56,79.8,79.88,80,80.88,81.06,81.38,81.82,82.02,82.24]},{"s":3,"a":82.85,"b":88.48,"text":"Same features, different experience. That difference is the work of a UX designer.","w":[82.98,83.34,83.98,84.34,86.02,86.28,86.82,86.94,87.06,87.3,87.42,87.62,87.96]},{"s":4,"a":89.33,"b":94.32,"text":"Quick check. Think about the colour and shape of a button. Is that UI or UX?","w":[89.38,89.62,90.42,90.62,90.8,90.94,91.32,91.46,91.72,91.84,91.9,92.8,92.92,93.28,93.66,93.88]},{"s":4,"a":94.77,"b":99.81,"text":"Now think about whether people can find that button when they need it. Is that UI or UX?","w":[94.82,95.06,95.32,95.56,95.84,96.16,96.32,96.56,96.74,97.02,97.16,97.3,97.5,98.14,98.24,98.54,99.04,99.26]},{"s":4,"a":100.26,"b":102.52,"text":"Pause here and try it. I'll wait.","w":[100.3,100.62,100.92,101.06,101.34,101.96,102.14]},{"s":5,"a":103.37,"b":107.77,"text":"The look is UI. Being able to find and use it is UX.","w":[103.38,103.54,103.86,104.12,105,105.28,105.48,105.68,106.14,106.32,106.5,106.98,107.22]},{"s":5,"a":108.07,"b":112.94,"text":"One is the surface you see and touch. The other is the whole experience of reaching your goal.","w":[108.22,108.38,108.48,108.6,108.96,109.14,109.44,109.56,110.44,110.62,110.96,111.06,111.18,111.42,112,112.14,112.46,112.62]},{"s":6,"a":113.79,"b":120.46,"text":"One mistake is thinking UX means making things pretty. Pretty helps, but clear and easy use matters more.","w":[113.94,114.1,114.56,114.68,115.3,115.7,116.02,116.36,116.7,117.56,117.84,118.5,118.72,119.1,119.32,119.62,119.82,120.16]},{"s":6,"a":120.76,"b":127.83,"text":"Another is designing for yourself. Remember, you are not the user, so watch real users and decide from what they do.","w":[120.86,121.38,121.5,122.02,122.16,123.1,123.98,124.14,124.28,124.48,124.7,125.32,125.52,125.82,126.16,126.56,126.68,127.12,127.28,127.44,127.62]},{"s":6,"a":128.13,"b":134.29,"text":"Two more mistakes are adding features instead of removing friction, and skipping testing. Test early, and repeat.","w":[128.18,128.38,128.58,129.04,129.18,129.44,129.92,130.22,130.32,130.72,131.28,131.42,131.76,132.84,133.16,133.7,133.84]},{"s":7,"a":135.14,"b":141.69,"text":"Recap. UX is how a product feels from start to finish. UI is the part you see and touch.","w":[135.24,136.26,136.86,136.98,137.14,137.24,137.66,138.02,138.26,138.54,138.66,139.66,140.12,140.22,140.34,140.6,140.82,141.12,141.26]},{"s":7,"a":141.99,"b":150.76,"text":"Good UX is useful, usable and accessible. The process is understand, define, sketch, prototype, test, and repeat.","w":[142.02,142.36,142.74,142.94,143.9,144.6,144.74,145.92,146.06,146.54,146.74,147.52,148.22,148.94,149.74,150.18,150.32]},{"s":7,"a":151.06,"b":156.53,"text":"Watch users instead of guessing. Test early, and remove friction before adding features.","w":[151.14,151.5,151.94,152.26,152.36,153.32,153.7,154.4,154.54,154.92,155.36,155.7,155.94]},{"s":7,"a":156.83,"b":162.2,"text":"Top tip: when a screen looks fine but still confuses people, fix the experience, not just the colour.","w":[156.86,157.18,157.8,157.98,158.06,158.4,158.66,158.98,159.16,159.42,159.96,160.4,160.64,160.76,161.4,161.6,161.78,161.88]},{"s":7,"a":162.5,"b":165.06,"text":"Knowzone is here whenever you want to keep learning.","w":[162.58,163.18,163.32,163.6,164.06,164.22,164.42,164.54,164.74]}],"scenes":[{"at":0.25,"heading":"Looks fine, still fails","items":[{"at":0.4,"kind":"text","text":"Lovely app, but want to give up?"},{"at":5.7,"kind":"text","text":"Today's question:"},{"at":7.91,"kind":"text","text":"What is UX design? Why does it matter?"}]},{"at":12.7,"heading":"UX defined","items":[{"at":12.85,"kind":"term","text":"UX = user experience","detail":"How it feels to use a product from start to finish"},{"at":18.27,"kind":"text","text":"Can you reach your goal easily?"},{"at":24.79,"kind":"text","text":"Useful + usable: easy to learn, hard to get wrong"},{"at":30.2,"kind":"text","text":"Accessible: different abilities can use it"}]},{"at":34.66,"heading":"UI vs UX","items":[{"at":34.81,"kind":"term","text":"UI = user interface","detail":"Screens, buttons, text and colours you see and touch"},{"at":40.06,"kind":"text","text":"UI is one part of UX"},{"at":45.72,"kind":"text","text":"Lovely form loses everything you typed"}]},{"at":50.82,"heading":"UX process","items":[{"at":50.97,"kind":"text","text":"Understand → define → sketch → prototype → test → repeat"},{"at":59.92,"kind":"text","text":"Designer ≠ user: watch users, don't guess"},{"at":65.3,"kind":"text","text":"Don Norman popularised 'user experience' in 1990s"}]},{"at":71.38,"heading":"Example: money apps","items":[{"at":71.53,"kind":"text","text":"App 1: 9 taps + confusing error"},{"at":77.12,"kind":"text","text":"App 2: 3 taps, confirms receiver, clear error"},{"at":82.75,"kind":"text","text":"Same features, different experience = UX work"}]},{"at":88.91,"heading":"Quick check","items":[{"at":88.91,"kind":"question","text":"Button colour and shape: UI or UX? Finding and using the button: UI or UX?"}]},{"at":103.12,"heading":"Answer","items":[{"at":103.27,"kind":"text","text":"Look and touch = UI; find and use = UX"},{"at":107.97,"kind":"text","text":"UI = surface; UX = whole experience to goal"}]},{"at":113.54,"heading":"Common mistakes","items":[{"at":113.69,"kind":"wrong","text":"UX = making things pretty"},{"at":120.66,"kind":"wrong","text":"Design for yourself"},{"at":128.03,"kind":"wrong","text":"Add features instead of removing friction"},{"at":128.03,"kind":"wrong","text":"Skip testing"}]},{"at":134.89,"heading":"Recap & top tip","items":[{"at":135.04,"kind":"text","text":"UX = feel start to finish; UI = see and touch"},{"at":141.89,"kind":"text","text":"Useful, usable, accessible"},{"at":141.89,"kind":"text","text":"Understand → define → sketch → prototype → test → repeat"},{"at":150.96,"kind":"text","text":"Watch users; test early; remove friction first"},{"at":156.73,"kind":"tip","text":"Looks fine but confuses? Fix experience, not just colour"}]}],"check":{"at":102.77,"seconds":10,"question":"Button colour and shape: UI or UX? Finding and using the button: UI or UX?","answer":"Colour and shape = UI; finding and using it = UX."},"fps":30,"mouth":"","level":"","credits":[],"voice":"qwen3-tts-12hz-1.7b (cloned voice)"}